 "final_text": "Answer submitted. Here's the summary for Robin:\n\n**What the return undoes:** ACH receipt **LHPAY-77** (voucher LHV-077, dated 2026-02-24), for **$18,000.00**, which had been applied in full against invoice **LHINV-001** (\"January platform fees,\" $18,000, due 2026-02-14). The ERP still shows LHINV-001 as closed/fully paid \u2014 it hasn't processed this morning's return yet, so once it does, LHINV-001 reopens at its full $18,000 balance.\n\n**What Lamna actually owes right now:**\n- ERP-recorded open AR today (not yet reflecting the return): $9,500 (LHINV-002) + $7,700 (LHINV-003) = $17,200\n- Plus the $18,000 reopening from the bounced payment on LHINV-001\n- **True open balance: $35,200**\n\nNote: I couldn't find any bank-file/return notice in email (the inbox returned zero messages in this environment), so this is built entirely from the ERP subledger (CustomerTransactions + CustomerSettlements for account US-021, Lamna Healthcare Company) \u2014 cross-checked by two independent verification passes that both landed on identical figures.",
